<h1>HD Format Element Specification</h1>

<p>For each allowed element, this document records whether the element round-trips losslessly to Markdown via the <strong>Copy as Markdown</strong> command, or whether it requires a lossy translation or raw-HTML emission. This is the authoritative reference consumed by <code>src/conversion/hdToMd.ts</code>.</p>

<h2>Round-trip status legend</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Lossless</strong> — Markdown has a native syntax that preserves all relevant attributes.</li>
  <li><strong>Lossy</strong> — Markdown can represent the element but loses some attributes (e.g., colspan, inline styles, classes).</li>
  <li><strong>Raw HTML</strong> — Markdown has no equivalent; the element is emitted as raw HTML inside the Markdown output.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Element matrix</h2>

<table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Element</th>
      <th>MD Status</th>
      <th>Notes</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>h1</code>–<code>h6</code></td><td>Lossless</td><td>ATX headings (<code>#</code>...<code>######</code>).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>p</code></td><td>Lossless</td><td>Plain paragraph.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>strong</code>, <code>b</code></td><td>Lossless</td><td>Both map to <code>**…**</code>; the strong/b distinction is lost.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>em</code>, <code>i</code></td><td>Lossless</td><td>Both map to <code>*…*</code>; the em/i distinction is lost.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>u</code></td><td>Raw HTML</td><td>Markdown has no underline syntax.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>s</code></td><td>Raw HTML</td><td>GFM has <code>~~…~~</code> for strikethrough; turndown emits raw HTML by default.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>code</code> (inline)</td><td>Lossless</td><td>Backticks.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>pre</code> + <code>code</code></td><td>Lossless</td><td>Fenced code block. <code>class="language-…"</code> is preserved as the info string.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>blockquote</code></td><td>Lossless</td><td>Lines prefixed with <code>&gt;</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>ul</code>, <code>ol</code>, <code>li</code></td><td>Lossless</td><td>Bulleted/numbered lists. <code>ol</code>'s <code>start</code> attribute is supported in GFM.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>dl</code>, <code>dt</code>, <code>dd</code></td><td>Raw HTML</td><td>No standard Markdown for definition lists.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>a</code></td><td>Lossless</td><td><code>[text](href)</code>. <code>target</code> and <code>rel</code> are dropped.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>img</code></td><td>Lossy</td><td><code>![alt](src)</code>. <code>width</code>, <code>height</code>, <code>loading</code> are dropped.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>hr</code></td><td>Lossless</td><td><code>---</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>br</code></td><td>Lossless</td><td>Backslash line break or trailing spaces.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>table</code> (simple)</td><td>Lossy</td><td>GFM table syntax. No colspan/rowspan, no multi-paragraph cells, no inline styles.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>table</code> (complex)</td><td>Raw HTML</td><td>Tables with colspan/rowspan, merged cells, or block content in cells are emitted as HTML.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>thead</code>, <code>tbody</code>, <code>tfoot</code>, <code>tr</code>, <code>th</code>, <code>td</code>, <code>caption</code>, <code>colgroup</code>, <code>col</code></td><td>Lossy / Raw</td><td>Follow the <code>table</code> ruling: lossy when the table is GFM-representable, raw otherwise.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>div</code>, <code>span</code></td><td>Raw HTML</td><td>No Markdown equivalent.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>section</code>, <code>article</code>, <code>aside</code>, <code>header</code>, <code>footer</code>, <code>nav</code>, <code>main</code></td><td>Raw HTML</td><td>Sectioning elements have no Markdown equivalent.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>figure</code>, <code>figcaption</code></td><td>Raw HTML</td><td>Markdown has no figure/caption construct.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>mark</code></td><td>Raw HTML</td><td>No standard Markdown for highlight.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>sub</code>, <code>sup</code></td><td>Raw HTML</td><td>No standard Markdown.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>kbd</code>, <code>samp</code>, <code>var</code>, <code>abbr</code>, <code>cite</code>, <code>q</code>, <code>small</code></td><td>Raw HTML</td><td>No Markdown equivalents.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>details</code>, <code>summary</code></td><td>Raw HTML</td><td>Renders inline in some Markdown flavors; turndown emits as HTML.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>svg</code></td><td>Raw HTML</td><td>Inline SVG passes through unchanged.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Attributes that are always dropped when converting to Markdown</h2>

<ul>
  <li>Universal: <code>id</code>, <code>class</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>lang</code>, <code>dir</code>, <code>style</code>, <code>data-*</code></li>
  <li>Anchor: <code>target</code>, <code>rel</code>, <code>download</code></li>
  <li>Image: <code>width</code>, <code>height</code>, <code>loading</code></li>
  <li>Table cell: <code>scope</code>, <code>headers</code></li>
  <li>Ordered list: <code>type</code>, <code>reversed</code> (only <code>start</code> survives in GFM)</li>
  <li><code>details</code>: <code>open</code></li>
</ul>

<h2>Implementation reference</h2>

<p>The HD → Markdown conversion lives in <code>src/conversion/hdToMd.ts</code>. It uses <code>turndown</code> configured with <code>headingStyle: 'atx'</code>, <code>codeBlockStyle: 'fenced'</code>, and a <code>keep()</code> rule for every element marked <strong>Raw HTML</strong> above. The reverse direction (Markdown → HD) uses <code>marked</code> in <code>src/conversion/mdToHd.ts</code>; output is then sanitized against <code>src/format/allowed.ts</code> before insertion into the editor.</p>

<p>When this spec changes, update <code>src/format/allowed.ts</code> (the <code>MD_STATUS</code> map) and the <code>turndown.keep([...])</code> call in <code>hdToMd.ts</code> together to keep them in sync.</p>
